        "title": "Hitler's Obsession",
        "body": "Stalingrad — a city bearing Stalin's name on the Volga River — became the focal point of Germany's 1942 summer offensive. What began as a strategic objective became an ideological fixation that would consume an entire German army and mark the war's turning point.",
